From 68abfe2d0acd5a04551374b39d92b986548fc5a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jayneelatintel <jayneel.vora@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:14:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 19/21] Vulkan: early submit behind a host event, decode
 profiler, Hadamard and add+norm kernels for Intel

The new switches are off by default.

- Deferred submit: ggml_backend_vk_set_defer_submit holds back what
  graph_compute records, ggml_backend_vk_flush_deferred submits it.
  Both are exposed through the backend registry for dist-tp
  record-ahead (LLAMA_DIST_TP_RECORD_AHEAD).
- GGML_VK_DEFER_GATE=1: a command buffer recorded ahead is submitted at
  once and waits on a VkEvent that the CPU sets when the all-reduced
  data is written back. A command buffer that waits on the gate always
  marks it pending, and the synchronous device submits release a
  pending gate first (an empty last piece of a prompt chunk otherwise
  left a waiting command buffer that nobody released, and the GPU was
  reset).
- GGML_VK_FENCE_POLL_PAUSES=N: poll the fence every N pause
  instructions while waiting (default 1000).
- GGML_VK_GRAPH_PROF=N: per-window CPU and GPU timing ([vkgprof]
  lines), N windows per line.
- GGML_VK_FWHT=1: MUL_MAT_HADAMARD as a subgroup Hadamard transform on
  Intel too; =2 the shared-memory kernel, =0 neither.
- GGML_VK_ADD_RMS_FUSION=1: residual add and RMS norm in one dispatch
  on Intel too; =0 turns it off everywhere.
- GGML_VK_SUBMIT_BY_BYTES, GGML_VK_FIRST_SUBMIT_NODES,
  GGML_VK_SYNC_ONE_SUBMIT, GGML_VK_UMA_READ: submit batching and
  readback experiments.
- GGML_VK_RM_Q6K_INT: rows per workgroup of the Q6_K integer-dot
  matvec, 4 by default on Xe2-class Intel devices unless
  GGML_VK_RM_KQ_INT is set.
- A fence wait longer than 2 s prints the gate and deferred-submit
  state ([vkgate]).

test-backend-ops: one warm-up run of the whole perf graph before timing.
